{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>My strength and the song of Yah.</b> Rashi's explanation: and likewise every word, etc. — כל (all), כלו (all of it), and שלישים (thirds) upon כלו (all of it). That is, just as one says מעול עולו, so one says מכל כולו." "<b>And He was to me for salvation.</b> Rashi's explanation: He was to me for salvation. Do not wonder about the expression ויהי, that it does not say היה, etc. And likewise in Chronicles: 'and the children of Judah,' וימלוך עליהם רחבעם. This is difficult against Rashi, for even this verse itself is in Kings." "<b>This is my El.</b> Even though a person does not see a thing, he may say <b>זה</b> about it, as in 'for זה Moshe, the man' (this Moses, the man)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:57.547005105Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}